    scenario: "A conventional furniture design used laminated particle board (difficult to separate into components for recycling) with glued-on veneer (contaminating wood recycling streams). Cradle-to-cradle redesign employed solid timber joinery (easily disassembly for component recovery) with minimal adhesives, enabling complete material recovery at end-of-life. This design prioritised recyclability throughout development rather than treating end-of-life as afterthought.",
